Dear Ms. Duke,</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
I am writing to document the statutory basis on which the closure of R00087=
9-070126 was improper, and to place that analysis in the record alongside t=
he Department's pending disposition.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
The Department closed my request on the basis that it &quot;is not the cust=
odian&quot; of the requested records, with a referral to the Oregon Parks a=
nd Recreation Department. That determination has a specific meaning under O=
regon law, and the Department's use of it
 does not meet it.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
ORS 192.311(2)(b) defines &quot;custodian&quot; as &quot;[a] public body ma=
ndated, directly or indirectly, to create, maintain, care for or control a =
public record.&quot; The statute then provides a single exception: &quot;'C=
ustodian' does not include a public body that has custody
 of a public record as an agent of another public body that is the custodia=
n unless the public record is not otherwise available.&quot;</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
That exception is the only statutory route by which a public body in posses=
sion of a record may disclaim custody. It applies where the possessing body=
 holds the record as an agent of the custodial body. It does not apply here=
.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
My request sought the Department's own communications: correspondence betwe=
en DAS and OPRD, and between DAS and the Office of the Governor, that refer=
ence me. In creating, sending, receiving, and maintaining its own correspon=
dence, DAS acts as a principal on
 its own behalf, not as an agent holding another body's records. The agent =
exception in ORS 192.311(2)(b) is therefore unavailable, and DAS is the cus=
todian of those records by the statute's plain definition.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
The exception fails a second time as to the DAS=96Governor's office communi=
cations. Even where an agency relationship exists, ORS 192.311(2)(b) restor=
es custodial status when the record &quot;is not otherwise available.&quot;=
 OPRD is not a party to correspondence between
 DAS and the Office of the Governor and cannot produce it. A referral to OP=
RD cannot make those records available, which places them squarely within t=
he exception's own proviso.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
The same analysis governs any OPRD-authored record in the Department's poss=
ession. ORS 192.329(2)(a) provides that a public body's response is complet=
e when it provides access to or copies of all requested records &quot;withi=
n the possession or custody of the public
 body&quot; that it does not assert are exempt. The test is possession or c=
ustody, not authorship. A record prepared by OPRD and retained by DAS is a =
public record in DAS's possession and is responsive to a request directed t=
o DAS.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
I would also note that &quot;not the custodian&quot; is not an administrati=
ve convenience but a formal statutory representation. ORS 192.329(2)(d) pro=
vides that a response is complete only when the public body, &quot;[t]o the=
 extent that the public body is not the custodian
 of records that have been requested, provides a written statement to that =
effect.&quot; The Department has made that representation as to records in =
its own possession, created in its own name, in its own systems. I ask the =
Department to identify the public body
 for which it claims to have been acting as agent, and the basis for that a=
gency relationship, or to withdraw the determination.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
Accordingly, the closure did not constitute a complete response under ORS 1=
92.329(2). The lawful dispositions available to the Department remain those=
 I identified in my letter requesting reopening:</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
1. Production of the responsive records;</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
2. Production with any claimed exemptions identified on a record-by-record =
basis, with the specific statutory authority for each; or</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
3. An express written statement that the Department holds no responsive rec=
ords within these categories.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
I would prefer to resolve this at your level. I am setting out this analysi=
s now so that the record reflects it was available to the Department before=
 any further disposition was made.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
Thank you,</div>
